Task 1: Set Up Ansible for Network Automation
Subtask 1.1: Verify Ansible Installation and Configure Environment

First, let's verify that Ansible is properly installed and configure it for network automation.

    Check Ansible version:

ansible --version

    Install additional network collections:

ansible-galaxy collection install cisco.ios
ansible-galaxy collection install community.network
ansible-galaxy collection install ansible.netcommon

    Create project directory structure:

mkdir -p ~/network-automation/{inventories,playbooks,group_vars,host_vars,roles}
cd ~/network-automation

    Create Ansible configuration file:

nano ansible.cfg

Add the following configuration:

[defaults]
inventory = inventories/hosts.yml
host_key_checking = False
timeout = 30
gathering = explicit
retry_files_enabled = False

[inventory]
enable_plugins = host_list, script, auto, yaml, ini, toml

[ssh_connection]
ssh_args = -o ControlMaster=auto -o ControlPersist=60s -o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null -o IdentitiesOnly=yes

